Changes
=======

0.6
---

* [Fixed] A failure publishing to X or Mastodon no longer prevents the other platform from being attempted. Failed posts are logged, and the database records which platforms succeeded.
* [Fixed] Initialize the optional blocklist correctly when no blocklist.py is present, so matched articles can still be processed.
* [Fixed] Skip and log an article whose URL cannot be resolved, including redirect loops, while continuing through the feed. A feed fetch failure no longer prevents later feeds from being checked.
* [Fixed] DeprecationWarning on SQLite's conn.execute() with use of datetime
* [Added] `--no-publish` to check feeds and record articles without posting to X or Mastodon. Recorded articles are treated as seen on later runs.
* [Added] Optional syslog and webhook error notifications in config.yaml, with custom, Slack, and Discord webhook payloads. Notification failures do not interrupt publishing.
* [Other] Added Ruff checks to CI and automated tests for publishing failures, notifications, the missing blocklist, `--no-publish`, and redirect failures.

0.5
---

* [Other] Give Twitter uploads a filename tweepy can type [#118](https://github.com/freedomofpress/trackthenews/pull/118)

0.4
---

* [Other] Bumped to Python 3.11 baseline
* [Other] Explicitly added BeautifulSoup4 to requirements and encouraged its use in blocklists

0.3
---

* [Added] Expanded blocklist functionality to support blocking based on skipping a particular paragraph when checking or skipping an entire article using a `check_article` or `check_paragraph` function.
* [Removed] Old blocklist format using a `check` function. **This is a breaking change for any projects that are using this blocklist format.**
* [Performance] Improved HTTP session management when requesting feeds.
* [Other] Added linters (flake8, black, isort) and updated code to satisfy them.
* [Other] Switched to Poetry for dependency management.

0.2
---

* [Added] Support for posting to Mastodon.

0.1.11
------

* [Fixed] Unbroke Twitter support by switching to using the v2 API for posting Tweets. The v1 API was largely discontinued. You will need to ensure your API creds are valid for the Twitter v2 API or provision new ones.
